  "id": "DrugBank_DB01598 - MONDO_4522",
  "verbalization": "Imipenem, a broad-spectrum antibiotic, is implicated in the pathogenesis of peritonitis through a series of interconnected mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Imipenem is used off-label for conditions such as Campylobacter Fetus Infectious Disease and Endocarditis, both of which are associated with the use of Cilastatin, a drug that is also linked to Peritonitis. This indicates a potential pathway where Imipenem, through its off-label use, may contribute to the development of peritonitis in certain patient populations. The presence of Cilastatin in these contexts further suggests a possible role in the pathophysiology of peritonitis, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of drug–disease relationships and the need for further mechanistic investigation to establish a definitive link.",
